nodes.notes:
Shaped exactly like the Outlook trigger's output, HTML body and all, so the Code node below is exercised the same way it will be in production. Edit the body to try a different email.

internetMessageId is generated per run, and has to be. Dedupe is on that id, not on the body: with it hardcoded, the first run records the id and EVERY later run -- however you rewrite the email -- comes back duplicate=true and stops at 'Do nothing', with a perfectly healthy academic classification sitting right above it. conversationId is deliberately NOT generated, so repeated runs accumulate into one thread and follow-ups can be tested. Reset that thread with:
  DELETE FROM messages WHERE conversation_id = 'TEST-CONVERSATION-1';
